 "rulebook": "World Athletics Competition and Technical Rules, 2024 edition: TR 16 (the start: 16.5 the line, 16.6-16.8 false starts), TR 17.3 (lanes), TR 18.2 and TR 19 (the finish, timing); the distance is the 50 m of indoor athletics",
 "deviations": [
  "the distance: 50.0 m, the short sprint of indoor athletics, on an outdoor straight; not the 100 m",
  "TR 16.3-16.4 (starting blocks, crouch start): a standing start without blocks, the feet 0.02 m behind the start line; a robot of this build has no crouch start",
  "TR 16.6-16.8 (start information system): the start movement is measured on the robot instead of the blocks: the pelvis more than 0.05 m from its place at \"set\", or a foot reaching the start line; a false start disqualifies at once, there is no recall",
  "TR 16 (the starter's voice and gun): the robot has no hearing; the commands are shown by a start lamp beside the lane (red, yellow at \"set\", green at the gun)",
  "TR 17.3 (lanes): the lane is judged by the pelvis: its centre more than half a lane width from the lane's centre line disqualifies at once; feet on the lines are not judged",
  "TR 17 (a fallen athlete): a robot whose pelvis is below 0.4 m is down; it may get up and run on, but 10.0 s down in a row end the race (did not finish)",
  "TR 19 (photo finish): the time is the instant the leading point of the torso link's collision mesh reaches the plane of the finish line's near edge, interpolated between 1 ms physics steps",
  "TR 14 (the track): a flat straight of three 1.22 m lanes, the robot alone in the middle one; no wind",
  "a race has no time to beat; here the run counts only if it finishes within 30.0 s of robot time after the gun (this benchmark's qualifying time: a mean of about 1.7 m/s, beyond the walking gait)"
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Run the 50 m: wait for the starter's gun, then sprint down your lane until your torso reaches the finish line.",
  "rules": "World Athletics rules for the straight sprint. The lane runs along +x, 1.22 m wide, centred on y = 0. The start line is 0.05 m wide; its far edge is x = 0 and the finish line's near edge is x = 50.0 m. The start: \"on your marks\" at t = 0, \"set\" 2.0 s later, the gun between 1.2 and 2.2 s after \"set\" (fixed for this task, not announced). Your start movement is the first moment your pelvis is more than 0.05 m from where it was at \"set\", or the front end of a foot reaches the start line (x > -0.05 m, on the ground or in the air). A start movement before the gun, or earlier than 0.1 s after it, is a false start; so is a foot reaching the start line before \"set\". From the gun on you must keep your lane: your pelvis may not be more than half the lane's width from y = 0. You finish at the moment the leading point of your torso (not the head, arms, legs or feet) reaches the finish line; the time counts from the gun. You succeed with a valid finish within 30.0 s of robot time after the gun. A fall does not end the race: you are down while your pelvis is below 0.4 m, you may get up and run on, but 10.0 s down in a row end it. You fail on a false start, on leaving the lane, when down for 10.0 s, or when 30.0 s after the gun have passed.",
  "venue": "You stand in your lane facing the finish (+x), the front ends of your feet 0.02 m behind the start line, your pelvis 0.18 m behind it. The lane lines are white on a red track; there are two white finish posts beside the track at 50.0 m. You cannot hear the starter: a start lamp on a post 4 m ahead of the start line, 1.0 m to the left of your lane's centre and 0.8 m above the track, shows the commands: red from \"on your marks\", yellow from \"set\", green from the gun.",
  "difficulty": "The gun has to be seen, not guessed: moving early disqualifies and waiting costs time. Then 50 m in a 1.22 m lane: the walking gait covers 20 m in the time, the running gait has to be held straight for a quarter of a minute at a speed close to where it falls."
 },
